The method takes another `JSType` object called `that` and returns a boolean. The first part of the code checks if neither `this` nor `that` is an unknown type. If both are known, it returns the negation of `isEquivalentTo(that)`. So, if they are equivalent, it returns false; otherwise, true.

The second part handles cases where at least one is unknown. It uses the XOR operator, which means it returns true if one is unknown and the other isn't. If both are unknown, it returns false.

I should explain this logic clearly in the docstring. I'll start with a brief summary, then detail the behavior in two cases: when both are known and when at least one is unknown. I'll also mention the parameters and return value.

